{{also|Teeter}}
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈtiːtə/|lang=en}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|/ˈtitəɹ/|[ˈtʰiɾɚ]|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To tilt back and forth on an edge.
#: ''Adjust the feet if you can '''teeter''' the washing machine.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} To be [[indecisive]].
#: ''We '''teetered''' on the fence about buying getaway tickets and missed the opportunity.''
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} To be close to becoming a typically negative situation.
#: ''Despite appearances, the firm was '''teetering''' on the edge of bankruptcy.''

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|teeterer}}
* {{l|en|teeter-totter}}
* {{l|en|teeterboard}}

